insert into toti_private.editorial_posts(id,title,body,topic,photo_asset,published) values
('8cba132e-766b-55e8-a935-6ea3e5559a5d','The hook on the way home','A four-note pop hook feels different when its last note lands just after the beat. Hum it over a walking rhythm and listen for the version that stays with you.','Making music','LoungeVinylListening',true),
('38575e18-05f1-5c01-b465-c085f281b6e8','Leave the second verse open','Keep the first verse busy and strip the second back to voice and a soft pulse. The chorus can feel bigger without adding another instrument.','Making music','LoungeStudioMixing',true),
('66e80c10-ad26-551a-ae87-0d2838a0ec36','A breath before the chorus','Try leaving one full breath before a vocal chorus. A small pause gives the next line room to land, especially when the melody starts quietly.','Making music','LoungeConcertLights',true),
('b77a95c1-66de-5871-b83a-20586ed0a89e','The warm side of a record','Listen to the bass beneath a soul vocal before following the melody. A held note and a gentle drum fill can carry an entire phrase.','Making music','LoungeVinylListening',true),
('6c5013b1-7ebd-5ed7-9123-826ce2c1fb17','An open string between chords','Let one guitar string ring while the chord around it changes. That shared note can make a rough verse feel connected without another layer.','Making music','LoungeGuitarRehearsal',true),
('ac2b3e08-5e6a-502c-8d5c-b606b373b38e','Keep the first guitar take','Record two versions of a short guitar phrase: one careful and one relaxed. Compare the rhythm before deciding which performance has more to say.','Making music','LoungeMusicCorner',true),
('40b53b81-362f-5943-afe5-7ebe2eb56f8a','The piano does not answer yet','Play a jazz phrase that ends away from home. Leave two beats for the bass or drums before answering it with another chord.','Making music','LoungePianoMelody',true),
('6fa04482-b1e2-5013-a854-c0b6bb0a80df','A quieter last chorus','Try the last chorus below the volume of the first. Keep the harmony warm and let the rhythm section carry the energy instead of playing harder.','Making music','LoungeStudioMixing',true),
('0afb1e84-26af-5718-9f78-bc7ba2d5fb04','Let the bass start the conversation','Build a short bass line with one deliberate pause. Invite the next instrument to fill that space rather than doubling every note.','Making music','LoungeStudioMixing',true),
('73f082b2-6926-54f1-b1a0-63631428b5c7','Three notes for a rainy afternoon','Choose three notes for a brass melody. Change the length of each note before changing the pitches, and keep the phrase easy to breathe.','Making music','LoungeMusicCorner',true),
('e95be06f-503a-5adc-b1e9-4c66ccb2ec9d','A verse around one open chord','Start an acoustic verse with a single open chord. Move the picking pattern under the words until the lyric finds its own pace.','Making music','LoungeGuitarRehearsal',true),
('da77fe29-1a98-58f7-827a-0bae0f1b68a6','The harmony under the line','Sing a folk melody once by itself, then add a softer voice underneath. Keep the harmony moving only where the words need a little warmth.','Making music','LoungeMusicCorner',true),
('e717fbae-9103-5de3-bd85-9def0df97ed3','Sunday fingerpicking','Try a steady thumb pattern with a melody that arrives a little late. Let the bass stay patient while the upper strings find their way.','Making music','LoungeGuitarRehearsal',true),
('46614ba1-ffad-547f-af28-9b16568a43ba','A piano question in four bars','Write four bars that end with a question. Repeat the same shape with a softer answer and leave the sustain pedal up long enough to hear the silence.','Making music','LoungePianoMelody',true),
('43ab7c40-0eef-531a-a5b6-65cd9e4cbbb3','Save the strings for the lift','Leave the strings out of the first verse. Introduce one sustained note at the next chorus before deciding whether the arrangement needs anything more.','Making music','LoungeMusicCorner',true),
('eef6085b-9725-5bcb-89de-cbd2b09645d4','A rhythm from the crossing','Turn a familiar street rhythm into a drum-machine pattern. Keep a little unevenness in the first version so its origin does not disappear.','Making music','LoungeStudioMixing',true),
('baf51159-7f87-5ef1-9585-ca5fa147f4e7','One synth, three distances','Play the same synth line dry, close and far away. Change only the space around it, then choose the version that leaves room for the drums.','Making music','LoungeConcertLights',true),
('67bab46c-38f6-5f73-b829-c503bbc8bcb3','Let the loop breathe','Run a short electronic loop and remove one sound on every fourth pass. A missing hit can make the return feel stronger than another layer.','Making music','LoungeStudioMixing',true)
